From u571bc49ad5c5fb80 at groups.google.com  Wed Feb  4 22:20:45 2015
From: u571bc49ad5c5fb80 at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?b?VG9tYXN6IMW7w7PFgnRhaw==?=)
Date: Wed, 04 Feb 2015 22:20:45 +0000
Subject: Fscores() and observations with only NAs
Message-ID: <4FtlvjHwHok.ChKU4mc-oTkJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/4FtlvjHwHok/m/ChKU4mc-oTkJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I observed that when fscores() is called with argument full.scores=TRUE, values of factor scores (of about 0) are assigned also to observations that have no other value than NA on all variables used in the estimated model. It seems rather inconvenient to me. If regarding EAP or MAP estimators it can be justified as using only information from prior in absence of any new empirical information for these observations, fscores() behaves in the same manner also when ML or WLE estimator is selected. Generally I think that what most users would expected (analogously to most other IRT software) is assigning NAs to such observations (even if using EAP or MAP). Maybe at least a warning should be returned by fscores() if it detect such observations in the data.

