Hi Phil,

When comparing models with different number of factors in exploratory IRT, is mirt's anova() is equivalent to the formula (28) in the paper High-dimensional maximum marginal likelihood item factor analysis by adaptive quadrature? <http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11336-003-1141-x> This method is used to choose number of factors, as mentioned in Reckase's book Multidimensional item response theory (p. 218). Thanks.

